(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #107, remedied by the `Free` statement: before this,
 `Free` on a buffer was a silent no-op - the buffer is `mmap`'d directly
 (`_alloc_buffer`) and never registered in the heap table `HEAP_FREE` walks,
 so 40000 iterations of "declare a buffer, Free it" held roughly 160 MB
 resident throughout. `Free` now calls `_free_buffer` (unregister-if-
 tracked, always munmap), so memory stays flat regardless of how many
 iterations run.

 Reads /proc/self/statm itself, the same idiom the #108 fixer's tests
 564/565 use: field 2 is resident pages. Before the fix this printed a
 five-figure page count at even half this iteration count; the threshold
 is a wide margin under that, not a tight bound - it only needs to catch
 the regression coming back, not chase the exact byte count.)

a number called n is 0.
While n is less than 20000, a buffer called piece is "x", Free piece, increment n.

a buffer called statm is 256 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called procfile at "/proc/self/statm".
Read from procfile into statm.
Close procfile.

(Skip field 1 (total pages) up to the separating space.)
a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to statm's size and byte i of statm is not 32, increment i.
increment i.

(Accumulate field 2 (resident pages) one digit at a time.)
a number called resident is 0.
a number called digit is 0.
While i is less than or equal to statm's size and byte i of statm is not 32 and byte i of statm is not 10,
    Set digit to byte i of statm,
    Set resident to resident multiply 10 add digit subtract 48,
    increment i.

If resident is less than 5000
    Print "ok".
Otherwise
    Print resident.
